{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>For every firstborn is Mine.</b> For from of old the service was performed by the firstborn, because they were the most honored in their household and the prerogative of service belonged to them." "<b>On the day that I struck every firstborn, I sanctified them.</b> But the reason I required them to undergo redemption was that on the day that I struck [the firstborn] I sanctified them to Myself, so that they would not engage in lay labor at all — just as I forbade shearing and labor for a firstborn animal. And this I did in order to save them through the law of holiness, for they were not worthy of being delivered from the destructive agency of evil angels (Psalms 78:49), being the most honored among the people with the entire nation's responsibility dependent on them. And I said that they be redeemed in order that they pass to profane status, in that they would be permitted in lay labor."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:01.041336732Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}